     "tax",
     "guild",
     "route"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "In the janapadas and mahajanapadas the king, helped by councils and officers, collected taxes and kept armies. Some, like Vajji, were ruled by assemblies of leaders.\nSociety was divided into varnas and jatis (occupational groups), with different rights and duties. Craft and trade guilds grew.\nTrade routes such as the Uttarapatha and Dakshinapatha linked cities, and coins helped trade."
    }
